      "generated_answer": "The text states that the Florentine Academy, founded and continued by the Medici family (Cosimo and Lorenzo), was \"largely devoted to the study of Plato.\" Within the context of the Italian Renaissance and the revival of Platonic thought mentioned in the passage, this philosophy is known as Neoplatonism. While the text also mentions \"humanists,\" the specific focus of the schools described is the substitution of the scholastic Aristotle with the works of Plato.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
