      "generated_answer": "Opportunistic foraging refers to a strategy where resources are gathered as they are encountered rather than through a pre-determined or highly organized schedule. This approach typically involves a reactive response to the environment and relies on whatever food sources are immediately available. Consequently, it is characterized by a lack of rigorous preparation compared to more specialized or logistical foraging strategies.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
