      "generated_answer": "Frederick Douglass was a formerly enslaved man who became the most prominent leader of the **Abolitionist Movement**, dedicated to ending the \"crying curse of human bondage\" mentioned in the text. While he was influenced by the Second Great Awakening and the Enlightenment, his primary identity and life's work were defined by the movement to abolish slavery.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{D}.",
