      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is based on archaeological interpretations of Teotihuacán's urban layout, which featured high-quality stone masonry and sophisticated drainage even in residential areas. This led early researchers to believe the structures were palatial, when in fact they were standard apartment compounds for the broader population. This discovery is frequently cited as evidence of an exceptionally high quality of life compared to other contemporaneous Mesoamerican cities.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
