    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4555",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\nOh, shame on you, poor Winter King!\nWhat's this that you have done?\nIs 't not a very naughty thing\nTo snatch the kaiser's crown?\nNow you will have to stay away\nAlike from Rhine and Prague,\nAnd more than that-shame and dismay\nYour days and nights will plague.\nRight well you knew, and all the world,\nRight well they know this thing,\nThat Ferdinand alone can be\nBohemia's lawful king.\nSo come, dear Fritz, rouse up and go\nTo Ferdinand, your king,\nAnd beg him graciously to show\nFull pardon for your sin.\n\"Poor Winter King,\" seventeenth-century song\nWhich of the following best explains why the narrator mentions \"Rhine and Prague\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Because these were the capitals of the Winter King's empire.\nB. Because these were strongholds of the Holy Roman Empire, the narrator warns the Winter King to stay away.\nC. These are the birthplaces of the Winter King's parents.\nD. They are the locations where the Winter King's armies are stationed.\nE. They are the cities where the Winter King had his most significant victories.\nF. They are significant military posts within the borders of the Holy Roman Empire.\nG. These are lands that the Winter King lost in battle.\nH. These are territories where the Winter King has hidden his wealth.\nI. They are the cities where the Winter King seeks asylum.\nJ. They are destinations for the Winter King's planned pilgrimage.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The \"Winter King\" refers to Frederick V of the Palatinate, who held lands along the **Rhine** (the Electoral Palatinate) and was briefly King of Bohemia (centered in **Prague**) before being defeated and exiled. The song mockingly tells him he must \"stay away\" from these locations because he has been stripped of his ancestral lands and his newly claimed crown.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{G}.",
