      "generated_answer": "The provided excerpts—the description of the \"House of Darkness\" from the *Epic of Gilgamesh* and the discussion of divine judgment and the \"river of life\" from the *Maxims of Ptahhotep*—both deal specifically with the fate of the soul and the nature of existence beyond death. These passages reflect how early civilizations used religious frameworks to understand and describe what happens to humans after they die. Therefore, they are best understood as explorations of mortality and the divine order.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
