    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4578",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\nThe invaders had brought in wheat and other Eurasian and African grains; peach, pear, orange, and lemon trees; chick-peas, grape vines, melons, onions, radishes, and much more. A Spanish nobleman come to America could require his Indians to furnish his table with the fruits of his ancestors.\n—Alfred Crosby, historian, 1972\nWhat was the impact of this process on Europe?\n\nOptions: \nA. The population declined as a result of imported disease.\nB. The population declined due to the loss of traditional agriculture.\nC. The population declined due to the increased competition for resources.\nD. The population declined because of famine caused by the mass export of crops.\nE. The population increased due to the new trading opportunities.\nF. The population increased due to the increased diversity of crops.\nG. The population declined due to conflicts over the new resources.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **F**.\n\nThe passage describes the **Columbian Exchange**, which involved the transfer of plants, animals, and technology between the Old and New Worlds. While the text focuses on European crops brought to America, the broader historical process led to New World crops (like potatoes and maize) being brought to Europe, which significantly increased food security and caused the European population to increase.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
