      "generated_answer": "The timing of monumental construction at Ceibal is significant because excavations revealed that its ceremonial complexes were built as early as 1000 BCE, which is earlier than the major Olmec site of La Venta reached its peak. This suggests that Maya urbanism was not merely a derivative of Olmec influence, but rather part of a broader, synchronous regional development. Therefore, it challenges the traditional \"Olmec-centric\" model of Mesoamerican history.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
