    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4658",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\nHe contains all works and desires and all perfumes and all tastes. He enfolds the whole universe and in silence is loving to all. This is the Spirit that is in my heart, this is Brahman. To him I shall come when I go beyond this life, and to him will come he who has faith and doubts not.\n—The Upanishads, India, c. 1000 BCE\nBased on the quotation, which statement is true of the speaker's religion?\n\nOptions: \nA. The religion is focused on material wealth and success.\nB. It believes in multiple universes.\nC. It is a polytheistic religion.\nD. It believes in reincarnation into various animal forms.\nE. It emphasizes on the importance of community over individual faith.\nF. There is an expectation of an afterlife.\nG. Salvation is based on the correct completion of rituals.\nH. The religion rejects the concept of a universal spirit.\nI. The religion promotes atheism.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **\\boxed{F}**.\n\nThe text states, \"To him I shall come when I go beyond this life,\" which directly indicates a belief in an existence or destination after death. The passage focuses on the spiritual union between the individual soul (Atman) and the universal spirit (Brahman) rather than material wealth or ritualistic mechanics. Consequently, the expectation of an afterlife is the only statement supported by the provided quotation.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
