      "generated_answer": "The excerpted text is from the **Pennsylvania Personal Liberty Law of 1826**, which was the subject of the landmark Supreme Court case *Prigg v. Pennsylvania* (1842). Critics and the plaintiff argued that the law unconstitutionally interfered with the rights of slaveholders to reclaim runaway slaves, thereby undermining the **Fugitive Slave Clause** (Article IV, Section 2) of the U.S. Constitution. The Court ultimately ruled that federal law (the Fugitive Slave Act of 1793) trumped state laws that attempted to regulate or obstruct the recovery of fugitive slaves.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
