    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A**.\n\nBoth the Mongol and Persian empires were known for their relative religious and cultural tolerance; as the text notes, the Mongols allowed \"virtually all religions\" and different peoples to live in peace, mirroring the Persian policy of allowing conquered groups to maintain their customs. Other options are inaccurate, as the Mongols were not primary builders of large-scale monuments (B), and neither empire significantly revolutionized the legal status of women in a comparable way (C).\n\n\\boxed{A}",
