      "generated_answer": "The most accurate similarity between the French Revolution and the American Revolution among the provided options is the opposition to unfair tax systems. Both movements were heavily fueled by economic grievances—specifically \"taxation without representation\" in the American colonies and the heavy tax burden placed on the Third Estate in France.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
