      "generated_answer": "Based on archaeological and historical records, the development of civilization is consistently associated with social stratification and the accumulation of resources by a ruling class or elite group. While warfare and art vary across different cultures, the centralization and concentration of surplus resources are considered defining characteristics of complex societies. Therefore, the most accurate general statement is that wealth concentration is a recurring trait.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
