    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In the provided text, Beveridge argues that the \"rule of liberty\" (consent of the governed) does not apply to people he deems incapable of self-government. He emphasizes a \"duty to the world\" and a \"mission\" to provide \"civilizing government\" to these populations to save them from \"savage\" rule or other hungry imperial powers. This reflects the \"White Man's Burden\" ideology, which asserts that powerful nations have a moral obligation to oversee less developed ones.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{D}.",
