      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **H. neoteny**.\n\n**Explanation:** Neoteny (the retention of juvenile traits into adulthood) allowed for a longer period of postnatal brain growth, which was essential for the development of the increasingly larger brains seen in *Homo erectus* and later hominids. This delayed development permitted the brain to continue growing rapidly after birth, bypassing the physical constraints of the pelvic canal. Other options like encephalization describe the state of having a large brain rather than the developmental mechanism facilitating it.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
