      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(input_data[0])\n    m = int(input_data[1])\n    s = input_data[2]\n    \n    # The segments between '0's are independent because '0' resets all T-shirts.\n    # We split the schedule by '0' and calculate the required logo T-shirts for each segment.\n    segments = s.split('0')\n    \n    max_logo_needed = 0\n    \n    for segment in segments:\n        if not segment:\n            continue\n        \n        # Total T-shirts needed for a segment is equal to the number of non-zero days\n        # because each day needs a fresh T-shirt.\n        total_days = len(segment)\n        \n        # On days with '2', a logo T-shirt is mandatory.\n        type2_days = segment.count('2')\n        \n        # On days with '1', either a plain or a logo T-shirt can be used.\n        # We have M plain T-shirts available.\n        # Required logo T-shirts for a segment is:\n        # 1. At least type2_days (since only logo shirts work for '2').\n        # 2. total_days - m (since we can use at most m plain shirts for '1's).\n        \n        needed_for_this_segment = max(type2_days, total_days - m)\n        \n        if needed_for_this_segment > max_logo_needed:\n            max_logo_needed = needed_for_this_segment\n            \n    print(max_logo_needed)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
