imum of these differences across all divisors\n\nHowever, note that n can be up to 150,000, and the sum of n across all test cases is ≤ 150,000. But if we try all divisors of n and for each divisor do an O(n) computation, the total complexity could be high.\n\nBut note: the sum of n across all test cases is ≤ 150,000. And for each test case, the work for all divisors would be:\n- For each divisor k of n, we need to compute n/k truck sums, each of size k, so total work is n (since sum over divisors k of n of n/k = n * sum over divisors k of 1/k, but actually we just iterate through all elements once per divisor).\n\nWait, more precisely: for a given k, to compute all truck weights, we need to compute sums of consecutive k-element segments. We can do this in O(n/k) time by computing prefix sums first.\n\nActually, we can precompute prefix sums for the array in O(n), then for each divisor k, compute truck weights in O(n/k) time, and find min/max in O(n/k) time.\n\nThe total work for a test case would be O(n + sum_{k|n} (n/k)).\n\nBut note: sum_{k|n} (n/k) = sum_{d|n} d (where d = n/k), which is the sum of divisors of n. The maximum sum of divisors for n ≤ 150,000 is not too large (the worst case is highly composite numbers, but even for 134400, the sum of divisors is around 500,000 or so).\n\nGiven that the sum of n across all test cases is ≤ 150,000, the total work should be acceptable.\n\nLet me implement:\n\n1. Precompute prefix sums: `prefix[0] = 0`, `prefix[i] = a[0] + a[1] + ... + a[i-1]`\n2. Then the sum from index l to r (inclusive) is `prefix[r+1] - prefix[l]`\n3. For a given k, truck i has sum `prefix[(i+1)*k] - prefix[i*k]`\n4. Find min and max of these sums, compute diff, track maximum diff across all k\n\nLet's code accordingly.\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    t = int(data[0])\n    index = 1\n    results = []\n    \n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(data[index])\n        index += 1\n        a = list(map(int, data[index:index+n]))\n        index += n\n        \n        # Compute prefix sums\n        prefix = [0] * (n + 1)\n        for i in range(n):\n            prefix[i+1] = prefix[i] + a[i]\n        \n        # Find all divisors of n\n        divisors = []\n        k = 1\n        while k * k <= n:\n            if n % k == 0:\n                divisors.append(k)\n                if k != n // k:\n                    divisors.append(n // k)\n            k += 1\n        \n        max_diff = 0  # at least 0 for single truck case\n        \n        # For each divisor k (number of boxes per truck)\n        for k in divisors:\n            num_trucks = n // k\n            if num_trucks == 1:\n                diff = 0\n            else:\n                truck_weights = []\n                for i in range(num_trucks):\n                    # truck i contains boxes from i*k to (i+1)*k - 1\n                    weight = prefix[(i+1)*k] - prefix[i*k]\n                    truck_weights.append(weight)\n                diff = max(truck_weights) - min(truck_weights)\n            \n            if diff > max_diff:\n                max_diff = diff\n        \n        results.append(str(max_diff))\n    \n    # Output all results\n    print('\\n'.join(results))\n\n# Call the function\nsolve()\n```",
