      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we need to iterate through all possible divisors $k$ of $n$. For each $k$, we calculate the total weight of each truck by summing $k$ consecutive elements. We track the maximum and minimum sums among these trucks and record the maximum difference found across all valid $k$.\n\nTo optimize the calculation of block sums, we use a prefix sum array.\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    idx = 0\n    t = int(input_data[idx])\n    idx += 1\n    \n    results = []\n    \n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(input_data[idx])\n        idx += 1\n        a = [int(x) for x in input_data[idx:idx + n]]\n        idx += n\n        \n        # Calculate prefix sums to get block sums in O(1)\n        prefix_sums = [0] * (n + 1)\n        for i in range(n):\n            prefix_sums[i + 1] = prefix_sums[i] + a[i]\n            \n        max_diff = 0\n        \n        # Check all possible k that are divisors of n\n        for k in range(1, n + 1):\n            if n % k == 0:\n                current_min = float('inf')\n                current_max = float('-inf')\n                \n                # Iterate through blocks of size k\n                for i in range(0, n, k):\n                    block_sum = prefix_sums[i + k] - prefix_sums[i]\n                    if block_sum < current_min:\n                        current_min = block_sum\n                    if block_sum > current_max:\n                        current_max = block_sum\n                \n                diff = current_max - current_min\n                if diff > max_diff:\n                    max_diff = diff\n        \n        results.append(str(max_diff))\n        \n    sys.stdout.write('\\n'.join(results) + '\\n')\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    solve()\n```",
