      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumCoins(prices):\n    n = len(prices)\n    # dp[i] represents the minimum coins needed to acquire fruits from index i to n\n    dp = [float('inf')] * (n + 1)\n    dp[n] = 0  # Base case: no fruits to acquire\n    \n    # Process from right to left\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        # Option 1: Purchase fruit at position i (1-indexed)\n        # This gives us free fruits from i+1 to i+i (if within bounds)\n        free_fruits_end = min(n, i + 1 + (i + 1))  # 1-indexed i+1, can get next i+1 fruits for free\n        \n        # Cost of purchasing current fruit + minimum cost for remaining fruits after free range\n        cost = prices[i]\n        if free_fruits_end <= n:\n            cost += dp[free_fruits_end]\n        \n        dp[i] = min(dp[i], cost)\n        \n        # We can always choose to purchase any fruit, so we need to consider\n        # the possibility of not using the free offer optimally\n        # Try all possible purchases from current position onward\n        for j in range(i + 1, min(n, i + 1 + (i + 1)) + 1):\n            if j <= n:\n                dp[i] = min(dp[i], prices[i] + dp[j])\n    \n    return dp[0]\n```",
