      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumCoins(prices):\n    n = len(prices)\n    # dp[i] represents the minimum coins needed to acquire fruits from 1 to i (1-indexed)\n    # We'll use 0-indexed internally, so dp[i] is min coins to acquire fruits 0 to i\n    dp = [float('inf')] * n\n    \n    # Base case: to get the first fruit (index 0), we must buy it\n    dp[0] = prices[0]\n    \n    # For each fruit i (0-indexed), if we buy it, we get the next i+1 fruits for free\n    # (since i is 0-indexed, the fruit number is i+1, so we get next (i+1) fruits free)\n    for i in range(n):\n        # If we buy fruit i, we can get fruits from i+1 to min(i + i + 1, n-1) for free\n        free_end = min(i + i + 1, n - 1)\n        \n        # Update dp values for all fruits we can get for free after buying fruit i\n        for j in range(i + 1, free_end + 1):\n            dp[j] = min(dp[j], dp[i])\n        \n        # Also consider buying the next fruit (i+1) if it exists\n        if i + 1 < n:\n            dp[i + 1] = min(dp[i + 1], dp[i] + prices[i + 1])\n    \n    return dp[n - 1]\n```",
