    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countSubMultisets(nums, l, r):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    # Count frequency of each number\n    freq = {}\n    for num in nums:\n        freq[num] = freq.get(num, 0) + 1\n    \n    # dp[i] represents the number of ways to achieve sum i\n    dp = [0] * (max(r, sum(nums)) + 1)\n    dp[0] = 1  # Empty subset has sum 0\n    \n    # Process each unique number\n    for num, count in freq.items():\n        new_dp = dp[:]\n        # For each possible sum\n        for i in range(len(dp)):\n            if dp[i] == 0:\n                continue\n            # Add 1, 2, ..., count occurrences of num\n            for k in range(1, count + 1):\n                new_sum = i + k * num\n                if new_sum < len(dp):\n                    new_dp[new_sum] = (new_dp[new_sum] + dp[i]) % MOD\n        dp = new_dp\n    \n    # Sum up all valid sums in range [l, r]\n    result = 0\n    for i in range(l, r + 1):\n        if i < len(dp):\n            result = (result + dp[i]) % MOD\n    \n    return result\n```",
