    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countSubMultisets(nums, l, r):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    \n    # Count frequency of each number\n    from collections import Counter\n    counter = Counter(nums)\n    \n    # dp[i] represents the number of ways to achieve sum i\n    dp = [0] * (r + 1)\n    dp[0] = 1  # Empty multiset\n    \n    # Handle zeros separately - they don't affect sum but increase count\n    zero_count = counter.get(0, 0)\n    \n    # Process non-zero elements\n    for num in sorted(counter.keys()):\n        if num == 0:\n            continue\n            \n        count = counter[num]\n        # Update dp in reverse order to avoid overwriting needed values\n        # Use sliding window optimization for bounded knapsack problem\n        new_dp = dp[:]  # Copy current state\n        \n        # For each remainder modulo num\n        for rem in range(num):\n            # Use sliding window technique to efficiently compute sums\n            window_sum = 0\n            # We'll process indices: rem, rem+num, rem+2*num, ... up to r\n            indices = list(range(rem, r + 1, num))\n            \n            for i, idx in enumerate(indices):\n                # Add dp[idx] to window\n                window_sum = (window_sum + dp[idx]) % MOD\n                \n                # Remove element that's out of window (more than count occurrences)\n                if i >= count:\n                    window_sum = (window_sum - dp[indices[i - count]] + MOD) % MOD\n                \n                # Add current window sum to new_dp[idx]\n                new_dp[idx] = (new_dp[idx] + window_sum) % MOD\n        \n        dp = new_dp\n    \n    # Multiply by (zero_count + 1) since each zero can be included 0 to zero_count times\n    # This affects all sums (including 0) but we're only concerned with sums in [l, r]\n    multiplier = zero_count + 1\n    \n    # Sum results for sums in [l, r]\n    result = 0\n    for i in range(l, r + 1):\n        result = (result + dp[i] * multiplier) % MOD\n    \n    return result\n```",
