    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef medianOfUniquenessArray(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    total_subarrays = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    \n    # Helper function to count subarrays with at most k distinct elements\n    def count_subarrays_at_most_k_distinct(k):\n        left = 0\n        count = 0\n        freq = {}\n        \n        for right in range(n):\n            freq[nums[right]] = freq.get(nums[right], 0) + 1\n            \n            # Shrink window until we have at most k distinct elements\n            while len(freq) > k:\n                freq[nums[left]] -= 1\n                if freq[nums[left]] == 0:\n                    del freq[nums[left]]\n                left += 1\n            \n            # All subarrays ending at 'right' and starting from 'left' to 'right' have at most k distinct\n            count += right - left + 1\n        \n        return count\n    \n    # Binary search for the smallest value 'x' such that there are at least (total_subarrays + 1) // 2 \n    # subarrays with distinct elements <= x\n    # The median is the smallest value x such that at least half the subarrays have distinct count <= x\n    \n    low, high = 1, n  # minimum distinct is 1, maximum is n\n    \n    # We need the k-th smallest element where k = (total_subarrays + 1) // 2 (since median is the smaller one if even)\n    k = (total_subarrays + 1) // 2\n    \n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if count_subarrays_at_most_k_distinct(mid) >= k:\n            high = mid\n        else:\n            low = mid + 1\n    \n    return low\n```",
