    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    from collections import defaultdict\n\n    # Read input\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    \n    # Read parent information\n    parents = [0] * (n + 1)\n    if n > 1:\n        p_vals = list(map(int, data[2:2 + n - 1]))\n        for i in range(2, n + 1):\n            parents[i] = p_vals[i - 2]\n    \n    # Build children tree\n    children = defaultdict(list)\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        children[parents[i]].append(i)\n    \n    # Process insurances\n    covered = set()\n    \n    # Parse insurance data\n    idx = 2 + n - 1\n    for _ in range(m):\n        x = int(data[idx])\n        y = int(data[idx + 1])\n        idx += 2\n        \n        # BFS to cover x and up to y generations of descendants\n        queue = [(x, 0)]  # (person, generation_depth)\n        covered.add(x)  # The buyer is always covered\n        \n        while queue:\n            person, gen = queue.pop(0)\n            if gen < y:  # Can go deeper\n                for child in children[person]:\n                    if child not in covered:\n                        covered.add(child)\n                    queue.append((child, gen + 1))\n    \n    print(len(covered))\n\nsolve()\n```",
