      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_different_char_position():\n    S = input().strip()\n    \n    # Count frequency of each character\n    char_count = {}\n    for char in S:\n        char_count[char] = char_count.get(char, 0) + 1\n    \n    # Find the character that appears only once (the different one)\n    different_char = None\n    for char, count in char_count.items():\n        if count == 1:\n            different_char = char\n            break\n    \n    # If no character appears only once, then the different one appears at least twice\n    # but all others are the same, so find the character that appears less frequently\n    if different_char is None:\n        # Find the character with minimum count (should be the one that's different)\n        different_char = min(char_count.keys(), key=lambda x: char_count[x])\n    \n    # Find the position (1-indexed) of the different character\n    position = S.find(different_char) + 1\n    \n    print(position)\n\nfind_different_char_position()\n```",
