      "generated_answer": "To minimize the value $|max(nums1) - min(nums2)|$, we first sort the array `nums`. \n\nIf we sort the array in non-decreasing order such that $x_1 \\le x_2 \\le \\dots \\le x_n$, any partition will effectively result in a split point. If we assign the first $k$ elements to $nums1$ and the remaining to $nums2$, then $max(nums1) = x_k$ and $min(nums2) = x_{k+1}$. The partition value becomes $|x_k - x_{k+1}|$. Since the array is sorted, $x_{k+1} \\ge x_k$, so the value is simply $x_{k+1} - x_k$. To minimize this, we just need to find the minimum difference between adjacent elements in the sorted array.\n\n```python\ndef solve(nums):\n    nums.sort()\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n    for i in range(len(nums) - 1):\n        diff = nums[i+1] - nums[i]\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n    return min_diff\n```",
