    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given:\n\n- $ P(D) = 0.05 $\n- $ P(TP|D) = 0.99 $\n- $ P(\\neg TP|\\neg D) = 0.97 $ → so $ P(TP|\\neg D) = 0.03 $\n\nWe want $ P(D|TP) $. Using Bayes' Theorem:\n\n$$\nP(D|TP) = \\frac{P(TP|D)P(D)}{P(TP)} = \\frac{0.99 \\times 0.05}{(0.99 \\times 0.05) + (0.03 \\times 0.95)} = \\frac{0.0495}{0.0495 + 0.0285} = \\frac{0.0495}{0.078} \\approx 0.635\n$$\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{F}",
