    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the Bayesian network given below. How many independent parameters are needed for this Bayesian Network H -> U <- P <- W?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 10\nC. 2\nD. 8\nE. 14\nF. 12\nG. 16\nH. 4\nI. 5\nJ. 6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Bayesian network is structured as $ H \\rightarrow U \\leftarrow P \\leftarrow W $, meaning $ U $ has two parents ($ H $ and $ P $), while $ H $, $ P $, and $ W $ are root nodes (no parents). Assuming all variables are binary (2 states each), the number of independent parameters is the sum over each node of $ (k_i - 1) \\times \\prod_{j \\in \\text{parents}(i)} k_j $, where $ k_i $ is the number of states for node $ i $. For root nodes ($ H, P, W $), each needs $ 2 - 1 = 1 $ parameter; for $ U $ with two binary parents, it needs $ (2 - 1) \\times 2 \\times 2 = 4 $ parameters. Total: $ 1 + 1 + 1 + 4 = 7 $, but since 7 isn’t an option, the most plausible assumption is that $ W $ is a root with 2 states (1 parameter), $ P $ depends on $ W $ (2 × 1 = 2 parameters), $ H $ is root (1 parameter), and $ U $ depends on $ H $ and $ P $ (2 × 2 × 1 = 4 parameters), totaling $ 1 + 2 + 1 + 4 = 8 $.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
