      "generated_answer": "The forced-choice method presents raters with pairs of statements and requires them to choose the one that best describes the employee, which helps minimize subjective bias such as leniency or central tendency. This method improves the objectivity and reliability of performance appraisals by forcing distinctions among employees. While it may introduce challenges like ipsative measurement (where ratings are relative rather than absolute), its main advantage is enhancing reliability through forced differentiation.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
