    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is equal to one?\n\nOptions: \nA. The elasticity of the long-run aggregate supply curve\nB. The spending (or expenditure) multiplier\nC. The investment multiplier\nD. The balanced budget multiplier\nE. The aggregate demand multiplier\nF. The income multiplier\nG. The fiscal policy multiplier\nH. The money (or banking) multiplier\nI. The inflation multiplier\nJ. The interest rate multiplier\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The balanced budget multiplier is equal to 1, meaning that an equal increase in government spending and taxes leads to a proportional increase in equilibrium income by the same amount. This result arises because the spending increase directly boosts aggregate demand, while the tax increase reduces consumption by less than the full amount of the tax (due to the marginal propensity to consume being less than 1), leaving a net positive effect equal to the initial change in government spending. All other multipliers listed typically differ from 1 (e.g., spending/income/multipliers are greater than 1, money multiplier is usually >1, and elasticities or multipliers like the AD multiplier depend on slope parameters and are not inherently 1).\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
