    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5888",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Discuss how Adam Smith developed the concept of the divi-sion of labor.\n\nOptions: \nA. The division of labor suggests that workers should rotate between different tasks to increase job satisfaction\nB. The division of labor is a plan of production that separates work into many different tasks to take advantage of the specialization of labor.\nC. The division of labor was first proposed by Karl Marx in his book Das Kapital\nD. Division of labor was Adam Smith's term for dividing economic classes within society\nE. The division of labor is a method of organizing government duties among different branches\nF. The division of labor is achieved by distributing the workforce evenly across various industries\nG. Division of labor refers to the geographical separation of production stages in different countries\nH. The division of labor refers to the physical division of a company's labor force\nI. The division of labor is a process by which machines are assigned specific tasks to replace human workers\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
