    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Adam Smith introduced the concept of the division of labor in his 1776 book *The Wealth of Nations*, emphasizing how breaking down production into specialized tasks increases efficiency and productivity. He illustrated this with the example of a pin factory, where workers performing specific, repetitive tasks produced far more collectively than if each made a full product alone. This aligns best with option B, which correctly describes the division of labor as leveraging specialization to improve production.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
