      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **E**, as revisionists—most notably Eduard Bernstein—argued that socialism could be achieved gradually through democratic political action, trade unionism, and reforms within capitalism, rather than through violent revolution. This contrasted with orthodox Marxists who emphasized the necessity of class struggle and revolutionary overthrow of the capitalist state. Revisionists rejected deterministic predictions of capitalism’s collapse and instead advocated for pragmatic, incremental change.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
