      "generated_answer": "The federal budget deficit is the annual shortfall between government revenues and spending, while the federal debt is the accumulation of all past deficits (and surpluses). When the deficit is negative (i.e., there is a surplus), the government can pay down debt, so the debt decreases. Therefore, the correct statement is: when the deficit is negative, the debt decreases.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
