    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Proteins were shown to move about in a plane of the plasma membrane when mouse cellsurface proteins and human cell-surface proteins were observed to integrate along a fused mouse-human cell plasma membrane. Which of the following cell culture techniques was most likely employed in order to yield these results?\n\nOptions: \nA. Inserting a bacterial plasmid into a mammalian cell\nB. Producing a hybrid cell\nC. Injecting a fluorescent marker into the cell membrane\nD. Producing a heterokaryon\nE. Isolating an immortal variant cell from culture and using it to create a cell line\nF. Inserting a tumor-inducing virus into a normal cell to initiate transformation\nG. Using a method called cell fusion to combine the mouse and human cells\nH. Using a technique called transfection to insert new genes\nI. Using a process called somatic cell nuclear transfer\nJ. Inducing pluripotency in somatic cells to create stem cells\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The observation that mouse and human cell-surface proteins mix in the membrane of a fused cell indicates that the cells were combined into a single hybrid cell, allowing their membranes to merge and proteins to diffuse freely. This result is best explained by cell fusion, a technique where two different cells are induced to fuse and form a hybrid. The correct answer is therefore the technique explicitly involving fusion of mouse and human cells.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
