      "generated_answer": "To evaluate the constants $a'$ and $b'$, we use the conditions at the critical point: $\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial V}\\right)_T = 0$ and $\\left(\\frac{\\partial^2 P}{\\partial V^2}\\right)_T = 0$. By setting $P = \\frac{nRT}{V-nb'} \\exp\\left(-\\frac{na'}{RTV}\\right)$ and solving the derivatives at $V = V_c$ and $T = T_c$, one finds that $V_c = 2nb'$ and $a' = RT_c V_c / n^2$. For the molar case ($n=1$), these yield $b' = V_c/2$ and $a' = RT_c V_c$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
