  {
    "global index": "MathQA_782",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: each of 3 investments has a 20 % of becoming worthless within a year of purchase , independently of what happens to the other two investments . if simone invests an equal sum k in each of these 3 investments on january 1 , the approximate chance that by the end of the year , she loses no more than 1 / 3 of her original investment is\n\nOptions: \nA. 90 %\nB. 80 %\nC. 70 %\nD. 60 %\nE. 40 %\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given that each of 3 investments has a 20% chance of becoming worthless (i.e., 80% chance of *not* becoming worthless), and they are independent. Simone invests $k$ in each, so total investment is $3k$. Losing no more than $1/3$ of the original investment means she can lose at most $k$, which corresponds to *at most one* investment failing (since each failure loses $k$).\n\nProbability of 0 failures: $(0.8)^3 = 0.512$  \nProbability of exactly 1 failure: $\\binom{3}{1}(0.2)(0.8)^2 = 3 \\times 0.2 \\times 0.64 = 0.384$  \nTotal ≈ $0.512 + 0.384 = 0.896 \\approx 90\\%$\n\nThus, the approximate chance is **90%**.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 176,
        "output_tokens": 217,
        "total_tokens": 393
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
