      "generated_answer": "To solve this, note that each investment has a probability of $0.2$ of failing (losing $k$) and $0.8$ of succeeding (losing $0$). Total investment is $3k$, so losing no more than $1/3$ of it means losing at most $k$; this happens if either 0 or 1 investment fails. Using the binomial distribution $B(3, 0.2)$, the probability of 0 failures is $(0.8)^3 = 0.512$ and the probability of 1 failure is $3 \\times (0.2)^1 \\times (0.8)^2 = 3 \\times 0.2 \\times 0.64 = 0.384$. Adding these gives $0.512 + 0.384 = 0.896$, which is approximately $90\\%$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
