    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "For FM, the output signal-to-noise ratio (S₀/N₀) improves with modulation index β according to the formula:  \n(S₀/N₀) = (3β²) × (Sᵢ/Nᵢ)₀, where (Sᵢ/Nᵢ)₀ is the input SNR linearly.  \nGiven input SNR = 40 dB = 10⁴ (linear), the output SNR in dB is:  \n10 log₁₀(3β² × 10⁴) = 10 log₁₀(3) + 20 log₁₀(β) + 40 ≈ 4.77 + 20 log₁₀(β) + 40 = 44.77 + 20 log₁₀(β).  \nPlugging in β = 5, 10, 105:  \nβ = 5 → 44.77 + 13.98 ≈ 58.75 dB  \nβ = 10 → 44.77 + 20.00 ≈ 64.77 dB  \nβ = 105 → 44.77 + 40.415 ≈ 85.185 dB  \nThis matches **option A**.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
