    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To design the key, we check both shear and bearing stresses. Torque $T = 30{,}000~\\text{lb·in}$, shaft diameter $D = 3~\\text{in}$, so radius $r = 1.5~\\text{in}$. The tangential force is $F = T/r = 20{,}000~\\text{lb}$. Shear stress $\\tau = F/(L \\cdot t)$ and bearing stress $\\sigma_b = F/(L \\cdot w)$ (where $t$ = thickness, $w$ = width, $L$ = length). Testing Option C: $\\tau = 20{,}000/(2 \\cdot 1) = 10{,}000~\\text{psi} < 11{,}000$, and $\\sigma_b = 20{,}000/(2 \\cdot 1) = 10{,}000~\\text{psi} < 22{,}000$, satisfying both limits. Other options either exceed stress limits or are oversized; Option C is the smallest safe key.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{C}\n$$",
