    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10309",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the solution for the equationX=AX+bu;X(0) = X_0 where A=\\vert10\\vert,b=\\vert1\\vert,X_0 =\\vert- 1\\vert, \\vert- 22\\vert\\vert2\\vert\\vert0\\vert u(t) = \\delta(t) (impulse function).\n\nOptions: \nA. -3\nB. 2\nC. 0\nD. 3\nE. 10\nF. -2\nG. 22\nH. 1\nI. -10\nJ. -1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The given system is a linear time-invariant system described by the differential equation $ \\dot{X} = A X + b u $, with $ u(t) = \\delta(t) $ (impulse input), and initial condition $ X(0) = X_0 $. The solution after an impulse input is $ X(t) = e^{At} X_0 + \\int_0^t e^{A(t-\\tau)} b \\delta(\\tau) d\\tau = e^{At} X_0 + e^{At} b $, but at $ t = 0^+ $, the state jump is $ \\Delta X = b $, so $ X(0^+) = X_0 + b $. Given $ X_0 = \\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ -22 \\end{bmatrix} $, $ b = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\end{bmatrix} $, then $ X(0^+) = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ -20 \\end{bmatrix} $. However, interpreting the (poorly formatted) options and likely intent, the first component change from -1 to 0 suggests answer 0.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
