    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10309",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the solution for the equationX=AX+bu;X(0) = X_0 where A=\\vert10\\vert,b=\\vert1\\vert,X_0 =\\vert- 1\\vert, \\vert- 22\\vert\\vert2\\vert\\vert0\\vert u(t) = \\delta(t) (impulse function).\n\nOptions: \nA. -3\nB. 2\nC. 0\nD. 3\nE. 10\nF. -2\nG. 22\nH. 1\nI. -10\nJ. -1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The equation $X = AX + b u(t)$ with $u(t) = \\delta(t)$ implies $X - AX = b \\delta(t) \\Rightarrow (I - A)X = b \\delta(t)$. Given $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$, $b = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$, and $X(0) = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$, solving for the impulse response yields $X(t) = e^{At}X_0 + \\int_0^t e^{A(t-\\tau)}b \\delta(\\tau) d\\tau = e^{At}X_0 + e^{At}b$ (since $\\int_0^t e^{-A\\tau}b \\delta(\\tau)d\\tau = b$ at $t>0$). Evaluating at $t=0^+$, $X(0^+) = X_0 + b = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$, so the first component is 0, matching option C.  \n\n\\boxed{C}",
