      "generated_answer": "A. yes  \nThe study shows that c-kit expression increases with disease severity—from low/absent in mild hepatitis and cirrhosis to high positivity (82%) in HBV-related HCC—and correlates with histological grade and stage, suggesting its potential diagnostic utility in distinguishing advanced disease stages.  \nWhile not stated as a standalone diagnostic tool, the strong correlation and statistical significance (p<0.001) support its role as a helpful immunohistochemical marker in the pathological evaluation of HBV-induced liver disease progression.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
