      "generated_answer": "The study found a strong positive correlation between corrected QT dispersion (QTcD) and left ventricular hypertrophy (LVH) in hypertensive patients, with high sensitivity (92.9%) and specificity (98.2%) at a QTcD cut-off of 60 ms. This indicates that QTcD is an effective predictor of LVH in this population. Therefore, the evidence supports that QTcD can predict LVH in hypertensive patients.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
