    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Epicurus calls upon the atomism of **Democritus**. He uses this framework to argue that the universe formed not by divine design but by the eternal, law-governed interactions of atoms in void. This supports his aim of dispelling fear of the gods and death by grounding natural phenomena in material, non-supernatural causes.  \n\n\\boxed{Democritus}",
