    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The subsistence practices of people—how they obtained and used food and resources—are most directly inferred from the remains of animals they consumed, which are captured in the faunal assemblage from a site. While other options like geological layers or architecture provide contextual or environmental information, faunal remains offer direct evidence of diet and hunting or herding practices. Therefore, the best answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}",
