    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The passage describes young, low-wage female factory workers in late 19th-century New York enduring poverty, inadequate food, and exploitative working conditions—hallmarks of industrial labor during rapid urbanization and industrialization. This is most directly comparable to factory workers in the Industrial Revolution, as both contexts involve poor wages, unsafe conditions, and economic vulnerability, particularly among women and immigrants. While other options (e.g., coal miners, autoworkers) share elements of hardship, option D most precisely matches the era, setting, and labor conditions described by Riis.  \n\\boxed{D}",
