    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4498",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"His Majesty the Emperor of China agrees, that British subjects, with their families and establishments, shall be allowed to reside, for the purposes of carrying on their mercantile pursuits, without molestation or restraint, at the cities and towns of Canton, Amoy, Foochowfoo, Ningpo, and Shanghai; and Her Majesty the Queen of Great Britain, &c., will appoint Superintendents, or Consular officers, to reside at each of the above-named cities or towns, to be the medium of communication between the Chinese authorities and the said merchants, and to see that the just duties and other dues of the Chinese Government, as hereafter provided for, are duly discharged by Her Britannic Majesty's subjects.\"\nTreaty of Nanjing, 1839\nThe concessions offered in this treaty most directly created British\n\nOptions: \nA. colonies\nB. diplomatic embassies\nC. outposts\nD. vassal states\nE. militarized zones\nF. dominions\nG. trading companies\nH. protectorates\nI. spheres of influence\nJ. businesses\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Treaty of Nanjing (1842, not 1839) ended the First Opium War and granted Britain the right to station consular officers in specified Chinese ports for trade and communication. These arrangements most directly established British **spheres of influence** by securing economic access and extraterritorial rights in key Chinese cities without formal colonization. \n\n\\boxed{I}",
