      "generated_answer": "The oxygen isotope data from the Yok Balum Cave stalagmite reflects periods of decreased rainfall, particularly severe droughts, which correlate with the decline in Maya civilization activities. These droughts coincide with reduced construction at ceremonial centers, as construction required resources and labor that would have been strained during dry periods. This makes option D the most accurate response.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
