    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **G**. Silk was a luxury good heavily traded along trans-Saharan and Indian Ocean routes, with major production centers in China and India; its presence in West Africa indicates indirect trade connections with Asia. While other options (e.g., H for Muslims in court implying Middle Eastern links) point to trade, **G** most directly signals *Asian* trade since silk was primarily an Asian export to Africa and Europe.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
