    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The third stanza describes District Officers demanding land tax despite the fields being abandoned and crops in disarray, and the speaker laments, “where will it come from? You can't get blood from a stone!” This directly reflects the unsustainable burden of taxation on a depopulated, war-torn countryside, indicating that the state continued to collect taxes even as agricultural production collapsed—evidence of a strong, intrusive local bureaucracy enforcing fiscal demands regardless of hardship. Thus, the correct answer is **D**.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
