      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is $\\boxed{E}$. Voltaire’s critique in *Candide*—satirizing blind optimism (especially Leibniz’s “best of all possible worlds”) and exposing hypocrisy, cruelty, and irrationality in religion, politics, and philosophy—aligns most closely with Rousseau’s skepticism of enlightened absolutism and institutionalized religion, despite their personal rift. While Voltaire championed reason and reform, Rousseau critiqued the corrupting influence of civilization and aristocratic hypocrisy, sharing Voltaire’s Enlightenment-era distrust of dogma and institutional authority.\n\n$\\boxed{E}$",
